{"question_text": {"৪৮তম বিশেষ বিসিএস [স্বাস্থ্য] – মেডিকেল অংশ": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which is not a tributary of the inferior vena cava? ", "option1": "Right hepatic vein", "option2": "Left renal vein ", "option3": "Right suprarenal vein", "option4": "Left ovarian vein ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_270468198431750366699091.png\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which is the main support of the rectum? ", "option1": "Fascia of Waldeyers", "option2": "Puborectalis muscle", "option3": "Fascia of Dennonvilliers", "option4": "Perineal body", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_274374100441750366819553.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_694711640431750366813108.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is the artery of bleeding in duodenal ulcer?", "option1": "Superior mesenteric artery", "option2": "Superior pancreaticoduodenal artery", "option3": "Inferior pancreaticoduodenal artery", "option4": "Gastroduodenal artery", "answer": "4", "exp": "<u><strong>Relations of the first part of duodenum:</strong></u><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_458867438501750366953064.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_229002467431750365790842.png\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Lienorenal ligament of the spleen contains-", "option1": "Renal artery", "option2": "Renal vein ", "option3": "Tail of pancreas ", "option4": "Left gastroepiploic artery", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_876179354431750367048881.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Appendices epiploicae are present in-", "option1": "Sigmoid colon ", "option2": "Vermiform appendix ", "option3": "Caecum ", "option4": "Rectum ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_851556855441750367133387.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_188513604431750367125181.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which is the most superficial structure encountered within the parotid gland? ", "option1": "Retromanibular vein ", "option2": "Facial nerve ", "option3": "Superficial temporal vein", "option4": "External carotid artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_299133659441750367199476.png\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_476008205431750367179901.png\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Abdominal part of the right ureter is posteriorly related to-", "option1": "Root of the mesentery ", "option2": "Ileocolic artery ", "option3": "Right ilioinguinal nerve ", "option4": "Bifurcation of right common iliac artery", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_343403523431750367236495.png\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) The ligament of Berry of the thyroid gland is formed by-", "option1": "Levator glandulae thyroidae ", "option2": "Thyroglossal duct", "option3": "Pretracheal fascia", "option4": "True capsule of the gland", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_535987346431750367271551.png\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which is the homologous structure of scrotum in females? ", "option1": "Labia minora ", "option2": "Mons pubis ", "option3": "Hymen ", "option4": "Labia majora ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_693858344431750367324010.png\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which of the following structures lies most posteriorly at the hilum of the right kidney? ", "option1": "Renal artery", "option2": "Renal pelvis ", "option3": "Renal vein ", "option4": "Lienorenal ligament ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_303426912431750367494150.png\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which part of the male urethra is commonly injured during catheterization? ", "option1": "Bulbar urethra ", "option2": "Prostatic urethra", "option3": "Membranous urethra ", "option4": "Penile urethra", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_171373990431750367730351.png\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) The liver is divided into functional right and left lobe by the-", "option1": "Falciform ligament", "option2": "Middle hepatic vein ", "option3": "Ligamentum teres hepatis ", "option4": "Ligamentum venosum ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_630461620441750367857947.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_109335540431750367850710.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Reagrding the dermatomes, which is not true? ", "option1": "T4: Nipple ", "option2": "T10: Umbilicus ", "option3": "C6: Thumb ", "option4": "T1: Little finger", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_250986103431750367925788.png\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which is the independent sensory area of the radial nerve in the hand? ", "option1": "Tip of the thumb ", "option2": "Dorsal aspect of lateral three digits ", "option3": "Base of the thumb over the dorsum ", "option4": "Base of the thumb on the palm of hand ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_595903576441750368202253.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_477299854431750368195609.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Isolated sensory loss over the first dorsal web space of foot idicates- ", "option1": "Common peroneal nerve injury", "option2": "Deep peroneal nerve injury", "option3": "Superficial peroneal nerve injury", "option4": "Sural nerve injury", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_167019396511750368361602.png\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_557197306431750368320190.png\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which of the following features is not consistent with thick skin? ", "option1": "Present in the palm and sole ", "option2": "Has no sebaceous glands ", "option3": "Stratum lucidum is present ", "option4": "Has no epidermal ridges ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_764204817431750368505150.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Apocrine sweat glands are present in-", "option1": "Forehead ", "option2": "Axilla ", "option3": "Abdominal wall ", "option4": "Palm ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_368653225431750368676022.png\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which of the followings is an epidermal receptor? ", "option1": "Free nerve endings ", "option2": "Root hair plexus ", "option3": "Krause end bulbs ", "option4": "Pacinian corpuscles ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_657060618441750368837006.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) All of the followings are modification of the deep fascia except- ", "option1": "Flexor retinaculum of the wrist ", "option2": "Scarpa's fascia", "option3": "Psoas sheath ", "option4": "Planter aponeurosis ", "answer": "2", "exp": "Scarpa's fascia is deep layer of the superficial fascia of the anterior abdominal wall.&nbsp;<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_717778590431750369190501.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Capillaries with fenestrated epithelium and continuous basement mebrane is found in- ", "option1": "Bone marrow ", "option2": "Lungs ", "option3": "Choroid plexus ", "option4": "Spleen ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_437566059441750369318316.png\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_449430451431750369308032.png\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which is not true regarding veins? ", "option1": "Tunica media forms one third thickness of the wall", "option2": "Nutrition is mainly by vasa vasorum ", "option3": "Has thin adventetia ", "option4": "Has indistinct internal elastic lamina ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_651451225441750369534006.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-05104