/media/uploads/mceu_881472870431750372281900.png\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Central tendon of the diaphragm develops from- ", "option1": "Dorsal mesentery of the esophagus ", "option2": "Pleuroperitoneal membrane ", "option3": "Septum transversum ", "option4": "Dorsal mesogastrium ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_804626932431750372393158.png\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which cell is not present in the respiratory epithelium? ", "option1": "Type-I pneumocytes ", "option2": "Goblet cells ", "option3": "Grabule cells ", "option4": "Brush cells ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_122152153441750372597520.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which is not a site of natural constriction of the esophagus? ", "option1": "At the pharyngoesophageal junction ", "option2": "At the crossing with arch of aorta ", "option3": "At the bifurcation of the trachea ", "option4": "At the esophageal hiatus of the diaphragm ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_645021364441750372761427.png\" />"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) Anal canal above the pectinate line- ", "option1": "Is supplied by pudendal nerve ", "option2": "Develops from proctodaeum ", "option3": "Is affected by true hemorrhoids ", "option4": "Is supplied mainly  by inferior rectal artery ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_920814658431750373042377.png\" />"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Which group of axillary nodes are the first to receive lymph from the breast? ", "option1": "Apical ", "option2": "Medial ", "option3": "Anterior ", "option4": "Lateral ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img